  "notes": "よ is used to assert or emphasize information.\n\nFUNCTIONS:\n1. Assertion: {知|し}ってるよ (I know [assertive])\n2. New information: {電車|でんしゃ}が{来|き}たよ (The train has come!)\n3. Emphasis: {本当|ほんとう}だよ (It's true!)\n4. Advice/urging: {食|た}べなよ (Go ahead and eat)\n\nCONTRAST: よ vs ね\n- よ: asserts information the listener may not know\n- ね: seeks agreement, confirms shared knowledge\n\nCOMBINATION: よね\n- Combines assertion with seeking agreement: そうだよね (That's right, you know?)",
